 unread-count badge to the message entry and expose Messages, 3 unread to assistive technology. Hide the badge at zero, show 99+ above the cap, and verify count changes do not shift the navigation layout.\n\n### When to use it\n\n- Unread count\n\n🔔5✉12\n- New-content marker\n\nLAlex ChenOnline\n\nMMaya LeeAway\n- Online or offline state\n\nAllAwaiting payment **3**Awaiting shipment **12**\n- Small status attached to an icon or label\n\nL3Alex Chen has 3 new updates\n\n### When NOT to use it\n\n- Use a badge as the main content\n\nActive users12,846\n\nRevenue¥ 86.4w\n- Show a large number that no longer fits\n\nFrontend tasks\n\nDesign tasks\nA red dot means unread, not a category color\n- Rely on a colored dot with no accessible text\n\n🔔5✉9⚙2★7☰4\nIf every item has a red dot, nothing stands out as needing attention\n- Attach several badges to the same small target\n\n**Review declined**\n        View reason →\n\nAnatomy\n\n🔔5\n\n1BadgeThe whole badge, usually attached to a related element\n\n2HostThe icon, avatar, or text the badge is attached to\n\n3CountA number or red dot; counts above 99 usually display as 99+\n\nVariants\n\nCount\n\n🔔5\n\nWhen you have a few unread items that you want to explain clearly\n\nDot\n\n⚙️\n\nWhen you only need to indicate that there is new content\n\nStatus\n\nAM\n\nWhen an online or offline state should be visible at a glance\n\nOverflow\n\n✉️99+\n\nWhen the number of unread items exceeds the display upper limit, use the cap number.\n\nTypical use cases\n\nInbox count\n\n**VibeHub**\n      Components\n      Tutorials\n      \n      🔔5\n      ✉️99+\n\nNotification icon\n\nAlex ChenOnline\n\n      \nM\n        Maya LeeAway\n\n      \nBuild a botOnline\n\nOnline avatar\n\n📦 My Order3\n\n      \n🚚 Awaiting shipment12\n\n      \n⭐ My Collection\n\nNew tab\n\n**Good Finds**\n        🛒3\n\n      \nWireless Headphones Pro¥ 299\n          Add to cart\n\nRecommended tool\n[Web fine-tuning tool · Selector Pro\n\n## Select page elements for 